---
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { routes } from '../../i18n';
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';

const { company } = site;
const summary = [
  'The website is for information only. The properties shown are not an offer within the meaning of the Polish Civil Code.',
  'Using the website is free of charge and does not require an account.',
  'Full property details are shared after identity verification and a separate agreement.',
  `We handle complaints within 14 days. A message to ${site.email} is enough.`,
];
---

<Legal lang="en" route="terms" title="Website terms" summary={summary}>
  <section>
    <h2>General provisions</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        These terms set out the rules for using the website {site.domain} (the “Website”). They constitute the terms referred
        to in Article 8 of the Polish Act of 18 July 2002 on providing services by electronic means.
      </li>
      <li>
        The service provider is <strong>{company.name}</strong>, registered office at {company.address}, KRS {company.krs},
        NIP {company.nip}, REGON {company.regon}, share capital {company.capital.en}, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>{' '}(the “Provider”).
      </li>
      <li>
        The Provider operates as a real estate broker and holds the mandatory civil liability insurance referred to in
        Article 181 of the Polish Act of 21 August 1997 on real estate management: {company.insurance}.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Services provided through the Website</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        The Provider offers two services free of charge: access to informational content and preparation of an enquiry that
        the user sends from their own email app.
      </li>
      <li>
        The agreement for access to content is concluded when the Website is opened and terminates when the user leaves it.
        The agreement for preparing an enquiry is concluded when the form is opened and terminates when it is closed.
      </li>
      <li>
        Detailed property information is shared after identity verification carried out in
        accordance with the Polish Act of 1 March 2018 on counteracting money laundering and terrorist financing and after a
        separate agreement is signed, such as a brokerage agreement or a non-disclosure agreement.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Technical requirements</h2>
    <p>
      Using the Website requires a device with internet access and an up-to-date web browser. Animations and the enquiry
      form require JavaScript, and sending an enquiry requires a configured email app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Rules of use</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Users must not provide unlawful content.</li>
      <li>Actions that disrupt the Website or load it beyond normal use are prohibited.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Nature of property information</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Property information presented on the Website is not an offer within the meaning of Article 66 of the Polish Civil
        Code. It is an invitation to enter into negotiations within the meaning of Article 71 of the Polish Civil Code.
      </li>
      <li>Photographs and visualisations are illustrative.</li>
      <li>The binding terms of a transaction are set only by an agreement concluded in the form required by law.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The content, photographs, visualisations, logo and visual layout of the Website are protected by copyright. Copying
      or distributing them without the Provider’s consent is prohibited, except for permitted use under the law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Complaints about the operation of the Website can be sent to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </li>
      <li>A complaint should describe the problem and include the contact details of the person submitting it.</li>
      <li>The Provider handles complaints within 14 days of receipt and replies to the address they were sent from.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Personal data</h2>
    <p>
      The rules for processing personal data are set out in the{' '}
      <a href={routes.privacy.en}>privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Final provisions</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Matters not covered by these terms are governed by Polish law, in particular the Civil Code and the Act on providing
        services by electronic means.
      </li>
      <li>
        Consumers may use out-of-court complaint and redress procedures, including assistance from a municipal or district
        consumer ombudsman.
      </li>
      <li>
        The Provider may amend these terms for important reasons, such as changes in the law or in the scope of services.
        Amendments take effect on the day they are published on the Website and do not affect rights acquired before that
        date.
      </li>
      <li>These terms apply from {site.legalUpdated.en}.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Legal>
